<description>
Pack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.

Input structure
The grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms
separate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.

Rule
Build a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide
versions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned
rectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between
consecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a
bottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,
again separated by one background column.

Key insight
The input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object
contributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,
preserving left-to-right object order.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "solid monochromatic foreground rectangles ordered left-to-right",
  "dst": "packed upper wide slots and lower tall slots in the same left-to-right order",
  "match_cond": "rank(s) == rank(d) for both the upper and lower slot sequences",
  "transform": "paint each rectangle twice: min(h,w) by max(h,w) top-aligned in the upper band, and max(h,w) by min(h,w) bottom-aligned in the lower band, with one background column between slots",
  "grid_shape": "height 10; width is the sum of max(h,w) over source rectangles plus one separator column between consecutive rectangles"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  colors: 2 (bg = any color, fg = any different color)
  rectangles:
    count: 4-6 solid monochromatic fg rectangles
    dimensions: max(h,w) in 1-10, min(h,w) in 1-3 [observed]; h+w <= 10 (no band overlap)
    constraint: sum(max(h_i,w_i)) + N-1 <= 30 (output width fits ARC grid)
  input:
    height: max(max(h_i,w_i)) across all rects (3-6 observed)
    width: sum(w_i) + N-1
    layout: rects placed top-aligned in original orientation, 1-col bg gap between each
  output:
    height: always 10
    width: sum(max(h_i,w_i)) + N-1
    upper_band: each rect as min(h,w) rows x max(h,w) cols, top-aligned, left-to-right with 1-col bg gaps
    lower_band: each rect as max(h,w) rows x min(h,w) cols, bottom-aligned, left-to-right with 1-col bg gaps
    no_occlusion: REQUIRED; after normalization, no upper-band or lower-band rectangle footprints overlap each other
    remaining_cells: bg

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input structure is simple enough)
  steps:
    1. Pick 2 distinct colors for bg and fg.
    2. Choose N in [4,6]. For each rect, pick (h,w) with max(h,w) in [1,10] and min(h,w) in [1,3], ensuring h+w <= 10. Reject if sum(max(h_i,w_i)) + N-1 > 30.
    3. Build input grid with height = max(max(h_i,w_i)), width = sum(w_i) + N-1. Place each rect top-aligned at its column offset, with 1-col bg gaps.
    4. Build output as 10 x (sum(max(h_i,w_i))+N-1) bg grid. Paint upper band (short x long, top-aligned) and lower band (long x short, bottom-aligned) with independent column cursors and 1-col gaps. Reject any dimension set where the resulting output footprints overlap.
```
